<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">German East Africa Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> Company was a chartered company founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-peters">Carl Peters</a> in 1885 to administer and exploit the lands claimed through his treaties on the East African mainland. Its takeover of the coast leased from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Zanzibar provoked the Abushiri revolt of 1888 to 1889, which the German state had to suppress. In 1891 the company gave up its sovereign rights, and the territory became the colony of German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-east-africa-company.jpg" alt="German East Africa Company" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Author of the original drawing is unknown. Author of the SVG-interpretation: Fornax · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DOAG_Coat_of_arms_1900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
